 ## 2026-09-04
 
+### 2340 — Terminal manifest/probe/capability-evidence admission (leaf 2): mutant protocol caught a mis-targeted expiry test
+
+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-1zvmw7 on leaf-1 checkpoint `9481a20`. New: `internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go` (closed Manifest/Probe/Evidence schemas, 16-row capability registry, generation digest, rule 1–6 reconciliation, expiry, signature-verifier seam, operation gate, `Registry.AdmitProbe`); tests `manifest_test.go` (black-box, independent JCS/identity/RSA-signing recipe) + `manifest_pin_test.go` (white-box for parse-unreachable arms). Leaf-1 files touched only for a doc line and 3 added wire codes; no gate logic changed.
+- MUTANT PROTOCOL CAUGHT A MIS-TARGETED TEST: the "expired evidence" case re-signed mutated evidence (new ID) without refreshing the probe's `evidence_ids`, so under the original code it failed at liveness first (right arm, wrong reason to trust), and under a neutered-liveness mutant it failed at the ID-set arm instead of admitting — the test passed for the wrong reason and the mutant survived. Fix: every evidence-mutating case now calls `finalizeProbeIDs` after re-signing (6 cases + platform case), so each refusal lands on its intended arm; the corrected liveness mutant is killed.
+- DETERMINISTIC SIGNATURES DEDUP: RSA PKCS1v15 is deterministic per key+message, so a "distinct extra evidence" fixture built with identical fields was byte-identical and correctly deduplicated — the test was wrong, production right. Unreferenced-object case now varies a supplementary fact (`ui_absent`) to force distinct bytes; identical-duplicate acceptance is pinned white-box as the stated bound.
+- REAL PRODUCTION BUG FOUND BY TEST: strict decoder returned nil (not empty) slices for `[]`, so `json.Marshal` re-encoded them as `null` and omit-self identity recomputation diverged on claim-free/evidence-free documents. Fixed with non-nil array initialization; pinned by the empty-tuple admission test.
+- EVIDENCE: board outcome artifact `TASK-260830-1zvmw7_manifest-probe-evidence.md` — 12/12 mutants killed (each grep-confirmed present, compiling, red, reverted byte-identical), suite/vet/gofmt/tracecheck exit 0, package coverage 87.1%.
+
